      "writtenOn": "2018-11-01T22:12:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As part of that rebase, change this to not call exit() directly.  Instead have this return int 0 on success, negative on failure.  Have parse_parameters() pass on a non-zero or negative return value from parse_read_options(), so that the exit ultimately ends up being main() returning non-zero.\n\n(I don\u0027t fundamentally object to use of exit() btw, but I think once that other CL is submitted, avoiding exit() here will be cleaner and more consistent.  Also, avoiding exit() makes unittests for functions like this slightly simpler, should we ever write unittests for this.)",
      "parentUuid": "c76d8c69_ebacc07d",
      "revId": "6619d1d71aa7ceb7f60494c55c253ddbda2862f3",
